   "screen": "The keyboard up close",
   "title": "Figure 1.3.1 · The key groups on a full-size keyboard",
   "alt": "A drawing of a full-size keyboard with its key groups labelled. Along the top, the function keys F1 to F12. The large block on the left is the typing keys, letters A to Z and digits 0 to 9. To its right is the block of control keys: Insert, Home, Page Up, Delete, End, Page Down and the four arrow keys; Esc, Ctrl and Alt are control keys too. On the far right is the numeric keypad, laid out like a calculator. Special-purpose keys are outlined with a dashed border: Tab, Caps Lock, Shift, Enter, Spacebar, Print Screen and Num Lock. A legend at the bottom explains the shading for typing, function, control, numeric keypad and special-purpose keys.",
   "caption": "Groups are about what keys do, not only where they sit: Esc, Ctrl and Alt count as control keys, and Num Lock is a special-purpose key on the numeric keypad.",
