  {
   "screen": "Actuators, braille and other outputs",
   "title": "Figure 1.3.2 · A control loop: automatic irrigation",
   "alt": "A loop of four boxes joined by arrows going clockwise. Top left, the moisture sensor measures the soil (input). Its reading goes to the processor, top right; the arrow notes analogue to ADC to digital. The processor compares the reading with a pre-set value: if the soil is too dry it sends an OPEN signal, if it is moist enough it sends a CLOSE signal, to the actuator at bottom right, which opens or closes the water valve (output). Water flows or stops, reaching the soil and crops at bottom left, which get wetter or start to dry out. The arrow back up to the sensor says measured again. In the centre: repeats non-stop. Below: Sensors measure. The processor decides. Actuators act. Feedback: each new reading shows the effect of the last action.",
   "caption": "The loop never stops: the sensor keeps measuring, so the valve closes by itself once the soil is moist enough.",
   "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 400\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\"><defs><marker id=\"S1U3-2-gold\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0L10,5L0,10z\" class=\"f-gold\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"30\" y=\"40\" width=\"200\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-softb s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"65.6\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Moisture sensor</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"82.5\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-muted\"><tspan x=\"130\">measures the soil</tspan><tspan x=\"130\" dy=\"16.2\">(INPUT)</tspan></text><rect x=\"410\" y=\"40\" width=\"200\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-soft s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"510\" y=\"65.6\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Processor</text><text x=\"510\" y=\"82.5\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-muted\"><tspan x=\"510\">compares the reading</tspan><tspan x=\"510\" dy=\"16.2\">with a pre-set value</tspan></text><rect x=\"410\" y=\"236\" width=\"200\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-softok s-ok\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"510\" y=\"261.6\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Actuator</text><text x=\"510\" y=\"278.5\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-muted\"><tspan x=\"510\">opens or closes the</tspan><tspan x=\"510\" dy=\"16.2\">water valve (OUTPUT)</tspan></text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"236\" width=\"200\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-surface s-muted\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"261.6\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Soil and crops</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"278.5\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-muted\"><tspan x=\"130\">get wetter, or</tspan><tspan x=\"130\" dy=\"16.2\">start to dry out</tspan></text><line x1=\"232\" y1=\"77\" x2=\"406\" y2=\"77\" class=\"s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U3-2-gold)\"/><text x=\"319\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">reading</text><text x=\"319\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-muted\">analogue → ADC → digital</text><line x1=\"510\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"510\" y2=\"232\" class=\"s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U3-2-gold)\"/><text x=\"520\" y=\"156.4\" font-size=\"13\"><tspan x=\"520\">too dry?</tspan><tspan x=\"520\" dy=\"16.2\">signal: OPEN</tspan></text><text x=\"520\" y=\"196.4\" font-size=\"13\"><tspan x=\"520\">moist enough?</tspan><tspan x=\"520\" dy=\"16.2\">signal: CLOSE</tspan></text><line x1=\"406\" y1=\"273\" x2=\"234\" y2=\"273\" class=\"s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U3-2-gold)\"/><text x=\"319\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">water flows</text><text x=\"319\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">or stops</text><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"118\" class=\"s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U3-2-gold)\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"171.4\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\"><tspan x=\"120\">measured</tspan><tspan x=\"120\" dy=\"16.2\">again</tspan></text><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"175\" r=\"40\" class=\"f-none s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"171.4\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-muted\"><tspan x=\"320\">repeats</tspan><tspan x=\"320\" dy=\"16.2\">non-stop</tspan></text><text x=\"320\" y=\"346\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Sensors measure. The processor decides. Actuators act.</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"372\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-muted\">Feedback: each new reading shows the effect of the last action.</text></svg>"
  },
  {
   "screen": "Input, output or both? Putting it together",
   "title": "Figure 1.3.3 · Input only, output only, or both",
   "alt": "A Venn diagram of two overlapping ovals. The left oval, input only, lists keyboard, mouse, trackball, joystick, scanner, barcode reader, OMR, OCR, MICR, biometric scanner, microphone, webcam, sensors and graphics tablet. The right oval, output only, lists monitor, projector, printers, plotter, speakers, headphones, actuators such as motors and valves, and braille embosser. The overlap, both, lists touch screen, headset with microphone, multifunction printer, chip-and-PIN terminal, and game controller with vibration.",
   "caption": "A device belongs in the overlap only if it both takes data in and gives results out, like a touch screen that shows the display and senses your finger.",
   "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 380\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\"><ellipse cx=\"225\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"205\" ry=\"165\" class=\"f-softb\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><ellipse cx=\"415\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"205\" ry=\"165\" class=\"f-softok\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><clipPath id=\"S1U3-3-clip\"><ellipse cx=\"225\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"205\" ry=\"165\"/></clipPath><ellipse cx=\"415\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"205\" ry=\"165\" class=\"f-soft\" clip-path=\"url(#S1U3-3-clip)\"/><ellipse cx=\"225\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"205\" ry=\"165\" class=\"f-none s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"415\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"205\" ry=\"165\" class=\"f-none s-ok\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">INPUT ONLY</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">BOTH</text><text x=\"520\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">OUTPUT ONLY</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">keyboard, mouse</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">trackball, joystick</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">scanner</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">barcode reader</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">OMR, OCR, MICR</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">biometric scanner</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">microphone, webcam</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">sensors</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">graphics tablet</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">monitor</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">projector</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">printers, plotter</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">speakers</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">headphones</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">actuators</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(motors, valves)</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">braille embosser</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">touch screen</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">headset with</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">microphone</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">multifunction</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">printer</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">chip-and-PIN</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">terminal</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">game controller</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">with vibration</text></svg>"
  }
