  {
   "screen": "No display: a step-by-step diagnosis",
   "title": "Figure 1.5.3 · Diagnosing a black screen",
   "alt": "A flowchart of nine steps from top to bottom. 1, is the monitor on? Check the power LED; if there is no light, press the monitor's power button. 2, is the computer asleep? Move the mouse or press a key, then try the computer's power button. 3, is the data cable firm at both ends? 4, are the power cable and wall outlet OK? If there is still no light on a working outlet and cable, the monitor is faulty. 5, is the LED orange or flashing? That is suspend mode: wake the computer, reconnect the cable and restart. 6, try a different data cable. 7, turn up the brightness and contrast. 8, listen for POST beeps and note the pattern for the technician. A note says after every step, if it is fixed, stop. Step 9 is a decision diamond, the swap test, with two outcomes: if a known-good monitor works on your computer, your monitor is faulty and is often cheaper to replace; if your monitor works on another PC, the fault is in your video card or motherboard, so call a technician.",
   "caption": "Work from the simplest, most likely cause (power and cables) to the hardest. The swap test tells you which half of the system holds the fault.",
   "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 586\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\"><defs><marker id=\"S1U5-2-ink\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0L10,5L0,10z\" class=\"f-ink\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"20\" y=\"8\" width=\"290\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-softok s-ok\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"165\" y=\"27.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">After every step: fixed? Stop.</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"38\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"51\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U5-2-ink)\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"52\" width=\"290\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">1  Is the monitor on? (power LED)</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"97\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U5-2-ink)\"/><line x1=\"312\" y1=\"69\" x2=\"336\" y2=\"69\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/><text x=\"344\" y=\"73.5\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">no light: press the monitor&#x27;s power button</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"98\" width=\"290\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"13\">2  Is the computer asleep?</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"132\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"143\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U5-2-ink)\"/><line x1=\"312\" y1=\"115\" x2=\"336\" y2=\"115\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/><text x=\"344\" y=\"112.1\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\"><tspan x=\"344\">move the mouse or press a key;</tspan><tspan x=\"344\" dy=\"14.9\">then the computer&#x27;s power button</tspan></text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"144\" width=\"290\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"13\">3  Data cable firm at both ends?</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"178\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"189\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U5-2-ink)\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"190\" width=\"290\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"13\">4  Power cable and wall outlet OK?</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"224\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"235\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U5-2-ink)\"/><line x1=\"312\" y1=\"207\" x2=\"336\" y2=\"207\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/><text x=\"344\" y=\"204.1\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\"><tspan x=\"344\">still no light on a working outlet</tspan><tspan x=\"344\" dy=\"14.9\">and cable: the monitor is faulty</tspan></text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"236\" width=\"290\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"13\">5  LED orange or flashing?</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"281\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U5-2-ink)\"/><line x1=\"312\" y1=\"253\" x2=\"336\" y2=\"253\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/><text x=\"344\" y=\"250.1\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\"><tspan x=\"344\">suspend mode: wake the computer,</tspan><tspan x=\"344\" dy=\"14.9\">reconnect the cable, restart</tspan></text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"282\" width=\"290\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"304\" font-size=\"13\">6  Try a different data cable</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"316\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"327\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U5-2-ink)\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"328\" width=\"290\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"350\" font-size=\"13\">7  Turn up brightness and contrast</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"362\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"373\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U5-2-ink)\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"374\" width=\"290\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"396\" font-size=\"13\">8  Listen for POST beeps</text><line x1=\"312\" y1=\"391\" x2=\"336\" y2=\"391\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/><text x=\"344\" y=\"388.1\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\"><tspan x=\"344\">note the beep pattern</tspan><tspan x=\"344\" dy=\"14.9\">for the technician</tspan></text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"408\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"456\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U5-2-ink)\"/><polygon points=\"165,456 285,496 165,536 45,496\" class=\"f-soft s-gold\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"165\" y=\"492.4\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\"><tspan x=\"165\">9  Swap test:</tspan><tspan x=\"165\" dy=\"16.2\">which one works?</tspan></text><path d=\"M285,496 H308\" class=\"f-none s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><rect x=\"334\" y=\"422\" width=\"286\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-softbad s-bad\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"477\" y=\"440\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">A known-good monitor works</text><text x=\"477\" y=\"456.2\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-muted\"><tspan x=\"477\">on your computer: YOUR MONITOR</tspan><tspan x=\"477\" dy=\"16.2\">is faulty (often cheaper to replace)</tspan></text><rect x=\"334\" y=\"500\" width=\"286\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-softbad s-bad\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"477\" y=\"520\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Your monitor works on another PC:</text><text x=\"477\" y=\"536.2\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-muted\"><tspan x=\"477\">fault is in your VIDEO CARD or</tspan><tspan x=\"477\" dy=\"16.2\">MOTHERBOARD: call a technician</tspan></text><path d=\"M308,496 V452 H330\" class=\"f-none s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U5-2-ink)\"/><path d=\"M308,496 V532 H330\" class=\"f-none s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#S1U5-2-ink)\"/></svg>"
  }
