   "title": "Figure 2.1.1 · A PAN and a WLAN compared",
   "alt": "Left panel, PAN or personal area network: one person in the centre of a dashed circle of about 10 metres, linked by Bluetooth to a phone, a smartwatch, earbuds and a speaker. Right panel, WLAN or wireless LAN, such as Wi-Fi in a café or school: an access point in the centre sends radio waves (Wi-Fi) to two laptops, a phone and a tablet. A cable runs from the access point to a router, which connects through the ISP to the Internet.",
   "caption": "A PAN surrounds one person; a WLAN covers a building. Both are wireless, but a WLAN is still a LAN, linked by cable to the rest of the network.",
