   "screen": "Designing a small network",
   "title": "Figure 2.2.4 · A network design for the community centre",
   "alt": "A network diagram for the Castle Bruce Community Centre. Twelve desktops, each with a built-in NIC (six are drawn), and a printer are connected by Cat6 twisted-pair cable, with runs under 100 metres, to a 24-port switch that sends data only to the right device. The switch connects to a router. The router connects to a modem or ONT, which connects to the ISP and the Internet. The router also connects to a wireless access point using WPA3, with a separate guest network for visitors' phones. A UPS and surge protector keep the switch and router running through outages.",
   "caption": "Each part answers one need in the scenario: the switch joins the lab, the router and modem reach the Internet, the access point serves visitors, and the UPS protects against power cuts.",
