   "screen": "Footnotes, endnotes and breaks",
   "title": "Figure 4.1.4 · Page breaks, section breaks and a footnote",
   "alt": "Four pages of one report in a row. Pages 1 and 2 are portrait and in section 1, separated by a page break (Ctrl+Enter). Page 2 has a superscript 1 in its text and a matching footnote at the bottom of the same page. A section break (Next Page) starts section 2, which is a single landscape page. Another section break (Next Page) starts section 3, which is portrait again. A note says a section can have its own margins, orientation, columns, headers and footers, while a page break only starts a new page.",
   "caption": "To put one landscape page inside a portrait report, surround it with section breaks, not page breaks.",
