   "screen": "Active cell, Name Box, formula bar and fill handle",
   "title": "Figure 5.1.3 · What the fill handle does",
   "alt": "Left: copying a formula. D2 holds =B2*C2 for a juice order. Dragging the fill handle down fills D3 with =B3*C3, D4 with =B4*C4 and D5 with =B5*C5: the row numbers change as it copies down. Right: extending a series with AutoFill. Jan typed in one cell and dragged down becomes Feb, Mar, Apr, May. Other series: Monday to Tuesday, Week 1 to Week 2, and 1, 2 to 3, 4, 5 after selecting both cells first. Note: the fill handle is the small square at the bottom-right of the active cell; double-click it to copy a formula down as far as the data in the next column goes.",
   "caption": "The same drag gives a copied formula or a continued series, depending on what the starting cell holds.",
