   "screen": "Number and date formats",
   "title": "Figure 5.4.1 · The same value in different number and date formats",
   "alt": "The formula bar for B2 shows the stored value 1234.5. The same value displayed in six formats: General 1234.5; Number with 2 decimal places 1234.50; Comma style 1,234.50; Currency $1,234.50; Number with 0 decimal places 1235; Scientific 1.23E+03. A warning box explains the percentage trap: if a cell holds 15 and you click the percent button, it shows 1500%; type 15% or 0.15 instead, which stores 0.15 and shows 15%. Dates are stored as day numbers: the same date shown as dd/mm/yyyy is 30/04/2026, as d mmmm yyyy is 30 April 2026, as dd-mmm-yy is 30-Apr-26, as dddd is Thursday, and in General format is 46142.",
   "caption": "Formatting changes how a value looks, never the value used in calculations: 1235 on screen is still 1234.5 to a formula.",
