   "screen": "The primary key: one record, one identity",
   "title": "Figure 6.1.3 · Candidate keys and the chosen primary key",
   "alt": "A student table with five fields: StudentID, CXCCandidateNo, Email, FirstName and LastName. Three students: FHC0412 Kayla Richardson, FHC0413 Jaden Fleming and FHC0517 Kayla Richardson. StudentID, CXCCandidateNo and Email are labelled candidate keys, because each is unique for every record. FirstName and LastName are labelled not unique, because two students are both Kayla Richardson. StudentID is chosen as the primary key: short, assigned by the school and never changes. A good primary key is unique, never blank, stable and short.",
   "caption": "Every candidate key could do the job; the designer picks the best one as the primary key. A name can never be a key because it can repeat.",
