   "screen": "Multiple conditions: AND and OR",
   "title": "Figure 6.3.1 · AND and OR in the Query Design grid",
   "alt": "Top left, AND: Genre criteria \"Fiction\" and Price criteria >20 on the same Criteria row; both must be true, giving 2 records, Hurricane Season and Front Street Stories. Top right, OR: Genre \"Fiction\" on the Criteria row and \"Mystery\" on the or row; any row can match, giving 6 records. Bottom, the trap for \"Fiction or Science books under $20\". Left, wrong: \"Fiction\" with <20 on the Criteria row, but \"Science\" on the or row with no price condition, so Science books at $32.00 and $35.50 appear: 4 books. Right, corrected: <20 is repeated on the or row, because each row is a complete, separate set of conditions: 2 books, B003 and B012.",
   "caption": "Read each row of criteria as one complete question. Any condition you want to apply to every row must be typed on every row.",
