   "screen": "Choosing test data",
   "title": "Figure 7.5.3 · Normal, boundary and erroneous test data on a number line",
   "alt": "A number line of ages with the accepted range 10 to 17 shaded. Green dots at 12, 14 and 15 are normal data, typical valid values. Gold dots at 10 and 17 are boundary data at the edges, which should be accepted. Red dots at 9 and 18 are boundary data just outside, which should be rejected. A fourth card lists erroneous data, impossible or of the wrong type: -3, 150 and \"twelve\". Boundaries are where algorithms most often go wrong, so always test them.",
   "caption": "Test on both sides of each boundary: 10 and 17 must be accepted, 9 and 18 must be rejected.",
